    "answer": {
      "short": "\\$12 825 extra after tax.",
      "worked": "Last year, Luke was in the second tax bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess}&=34\\,000-18\\,200\\\\\\text{Excess}&=15\\,800\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=0+0.19\\times15\\,800\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=\\$3\\,002\\\\\\text{After-tax income}&=34\\,000-3\\,002\\\\\\text{After-tax income}&=\\$30\\,998\\end{align*}$$\nThis year, his taxable income is $34\\,000+16\\,800=\\$50\\,800$, in the third tax bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess}&=50\\,800-45\\,000\\\\\\text{Excess}&=5\\,800\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=5\\,092+0.325\\times5\\,800\\\\\\text{Tax payable}&=\\$6\\,977\\\\\\text{After-tax income}&=50\\,800-6\\,977\\\\\\text{After-tax income}&=\\$43\\,823\\\\\\text{Extra after-tax income}&=43\\,823-30\\,998\\\\\\text{Extra after-tax income}&=\\$12\\,825\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
